1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,260
Weeks before his comeback, Michael
Jackson was gone.

2
00:00:06,670 --> 00:00:10,920
This is what happened on the twenty
fifth of June, 2009, and what a court

3
00:00:10,960 --> 00:00:12,410
decided in November 2011.

4
00:00:15,830 --> 00:00:22,020
Michael Jackson was born on 29 August
1958 in Gary, Indiana, the eighth of ten

5
00:00:22,060 --> 00:00:22,750
children.

6
00:00:23,170 --> 00:00:26,370
The family lived in a two-bedroom house
on Jackson Street.

7
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:31,670
As a small boy he joined his brothers'
band, and he soon became the lead singer

8
00:00:31,710 --> 00:00:32,740
of the Jackson 5.

9
00:00:33,170 --> 00:00:39,270
In January 1970, I Want You Back became
the Jackson 5's first number one on the

10
00:00:39,310 --> 00:00:40,690
Billboard Hot 100.

11
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:46,740
Three more singles, ABC, The Love You
Save, and I'll Be There, also reached

12
00:00:46,780 --> 00:00:47,580
number one.

13
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:56,780
He broke out as a solo star with Off the
Wall in 1979, and in November 1982 he

14
00:00:56,820 --> 00:00:58,140
released Thriller.

15
00:00:58,570 --> 00:01:03,100
Thriller is widely regarded as the
best-selling album of all time, and it

16
00:01:03,140 --> 00:01:07,350
was the first to produce seven top ten
singles in the United States.

17
00:01:07,770 --> 00:01:12,570
In March 1983 he reunited with his
brothers to record the television

18
00:01:12,610 --> 00:01:18,070
special Motown 25, which NBC aired in
May to an estimated forty seven million

19
00:01:18,110 --> 00:01:18,650
viewers.

20
00:01:19,070 --> 00:01:23,470
There he performed the moonwalk, a dance
move the show helped make famous.

21
00:01:23,900 --> 00:01:28,670
At the 1984 Grammy Awards he won eight
awards in one night, a record at the

22
00:01:28,710 --> 00:01:29,000
time.

23
00:01:29,430 --> 00:01:34,570
On 14 May 1984, President Ronald Reagan
welcomed Michael Jackson to the White

24
00:01:34,610 --> 00:01:34,970
House.

25
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:39,100
Jackson had taken part in a campaign
against drunk driving, and the President

26
00:01:39,140 --> 00:01:40,080
honoured him for it.

27
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:43,960
Here is how the President introduced
him, in his own words.

28
00:01:44,370 --> 00:01:51,030
No, I know why you're here, and with good reason,
to see one of the most talented, most popular,

29
00:01:51,070 --> 00:01:54,330
and most exciting superstars in the music world today,
Michael Jackson.

30
00:01:54,370 --> 00:01:58,830
Michael, welcome to the White House.

31
00:01:59,170 --> 00:02:02,870
Reagan then read out the text of an
award, which he presented that morning.

32
00:02:07,300 --> 00:02:13,260
To Michael Jackson, with appreciation for the outstanding example
you have set for the youth of America and the world.

33
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:20,060
Your historic record-breaking achievements and your preeminence
in popular music are a tribute to your creativity,

34
00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:24,560
dedication, and great ability.

35
00:02:24,600 --> 00:02:32,060
The generous contribution of your time and talent to the
national campaign against teenage drunk driving

36
00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:38,560
will help millions of young Americans learn that
drinking and driving can kill a friendship.

37
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:40,320
Here is Jackson's reply on the South
Lawn.

38
00:02:40,930 --> 00:02:42,890
I'm very, very honored.

39
00:02:42,930 --> 00:02:45,290
Thank you very much, Mr. President

40
00:02:45,330 --> 00:02:48,790
and Mrs. Reagan.

41
00:02:49,130 --> 00:02:54,250
In 1987 his album Bad became the first
to produce five number one singles in

42
00:02:54,290 --> 00:02:55,490
the United States.

43
00:02:58,900 --> 00:03:03,700
By 2009, Jackson was fifty years old,
and he was planning a return to the

44
00:03:03,740 --> 00:03:04,100
stage.

45
00:03:04,530 --> 00:03:09,740
The plan was a run of fifty concerts at
the O2 Arena in London, promoted by AEG

46
00:03:09,780 --> 00:03:10,070
Live.

47
00:03:10,500 --> 00:03:15,080
The first show was due to open on 13
July 2009.

48
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:19,280
ABC News reported at the time that all
fifty shows were sold out.

49
00:03:19,700 --> 00:03:24,060
On the morning of 25 June, opening night
was eighteen days away.

50
00:03:24,470 --> 00:03:27,710
It was Thursday, 25 June 2009.

51
00:03:28,130 --> 00:03:32,350
At 12:21 in the afternoon, a call was
made to the emergency number from a

52
00:03:32,390 --> 00:03:36,130
rented house in the Holmby Hills area,
where Jackson was staying.

53
00:03:36,570 --> 00:03:40,190
He was taken to the UCLA Medical Center,
a few minutes away.

54
00:03:40,600 --> 00:03:43,520
He was declared dead at 2:26 in the
afternoon.

55
00:03:43,930 --> 00:03:47,130
His brother Jermaine Jackson announced
the death to reporters.

56
00:03:47,570 --> 00:03:50,090
News organisations tried to confirm it.

57
00:03:50,130 --> 00:03:54,570
CNN said the Los Angeles Times and CBS
News were reporting his death.

58
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:59,320
Here is the moment CNN's live coverage
reached the confirmation.

59
00:03:59,730 --> 00:04:02,290
I have to stop you for a second, A.J.

60
00:04:02,330 --> 00:04:05,490
CNN can now confirm from the LA coroner
that Michael Jackson is dead.

61
00:04:05,830 --> 00:04:09,290
Helicopter pictures showed crowds
gathering outside the hospital.

62
00:04:09,700 --> 00:04:13,160
His body was taken to the Los Angeles
County Coroner's office.

63
00:04:13,570 --> 00:04:15,570
The London shows did not go ahead.

64
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:20,330
How he died would take two months to be
named, and more than two years to be

65
00:04:20,370 --> 00:04:21,320
decided in court.

66
00:04:21,730 --> 00:04:25,910
The first goodbye came on Tuesday, 7
July 2009.

67
00:04:26,330 --> 00:04:29,630
A public memorial was held at the
Staples Center in Los Angeles.

68
00:04:30,070 --> 00:04:34,190
Nielsen counted about thirty one million
viewers in the United States alone.

69
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:37,900
Musicians performed, and friends and
family spoke.

70
00:04:38,330 --> 00:04:43,580
On Friday, 28 August 2009, the Los
Angeles County Coroner released its

71
00:04:43,620 --> 00:04:44,270
findings.

72
00:04:44,700 --> 00:04:47,500
The coroner ruled the manner of death a
homicide.

73
00:04:47,930 --> 00:04:53,030
The cause was acute propofol
intoxication, with the sedative

74
00:04:53,070 --> 00:04:56,770
lorazepam named as a contributing
condition.

75
00:04:57,200 --> 00:05:01,920
Propofol is a strong anaesthetic, used
in hospitals during surgery.

76
00:05:02,330 --> 00:05:07,390
In a coroner's report, homicide means a
death caused by the actions of another

77
00:05:07,430 --> 00:05:07,850
person.

78
00:05:07,890 --> 00:05:10,890
It is a classification, not a verdict of
guilt.

79
00:05:14,300 --> 00:05:17,670
The question left open was whether
anyone would answer for the death in

80
00:05:17,710 --> 00:05:17,960
court.

81
00:05:18,370 --> 00:05:22,630
The man at the centre was Conrad Murray,
a Houston cardiologist, and Jackson's

82
00:05:22,670 --> 00:05:23,690
personal physician.

83
00:05:24,100 --> 00:05:28,940
Two days after the death, on 27 June
2009, Los Angeles police interviewed

84
00:05:28,980 --> 00:05:32,120
him, and the jury later heard a
recording of it.

85
00:05:32,530 --> 00:05:36,750
Here is part of that recording, as
played in court and aired by ABC News.

86
00:05:37,470 --> 00:05:43,930
Murray's recorded police interview, played to the jury

87
00:05:44,470 --> 00:05:49,370
On 8 February 2010, Murray was arraigned
in Los Angeles on a charge of

88
00:05:49,410 --> 00:05:53,030
involuntary manslaughter, and he pleaded
not guilty.

89
00:05:53,430 --> 00:05:58,750
His trial opened on 27 September 2011,
and ran for about six weeks.

90
00:05:59,170 --> 00:06:02,890
Prosecutors said Murray failed to
monitor his patient closely while

91
00:06:02,930 --> 00:06:06,770
Jackson was sedated, and pointed to
phone calls he made that morning.

92
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:10,370
Murray's lawyers said he met his
professional duties.

93
00:06:10,410 --> 00:06:14,990
In court filings they suggested that
Jackson may have given himself an extra

94
00:06:15,030 --> 00:06:15,300
dose.

95
00:06:15,730 --> 00:06:21,040
On Monday, 7 November 2011, a Los
Angeles jury found Conrad Murray guilty

96
00:06:21,080 --> 00:06:23,110
of involuntary manslaughter.

97
00:06:23,530 --> 00:06:25,790
Here is the verdict being read in the
courtroom.

98
00:06:26,400 --> 00:06:29,560
We, the jury, in the above-entitled action,

99
00:06:29,600 --> 00:06:36,460
find the defendant, Conrad Robert Murray,
guilty of the crime of involuntary manslaughter.

100
00:06:36,800 --> 00:06:39,940
Afterwards, the lead prosecutor spoke to
reporters.

101
00:06:40,370 --> 00:06:47,030
Our sympathies go out to the Jackson family at this time
for the loss that they have suffered.

102
00:06:47,370 --> 00:06:52,780
Three weeks later, on 29 November 2011,
Judge Michael Pastor sentenced Murray to

103
00:06:52,820 --> 00:06:54,990
four years in jail, the maximum.

104
00:06:55,400 --> 00:06:59,800
The judge said Murray had shown no sense
of remorse, and that Jackson died not

105
00:06:59,840 --> 00:07:03,950
from one isolated incident, but from a
totality of circumstances directly

106
00:07:03,990 --> 00:07:05,280
attributable to Murray.

107
00:07:05,700 --> 00:07:10,950
Under California law, Murray served
about half of the sentence, and he was

108
00:07:10,990 --> 00:07:12,980
released on 28 October 2013.

109
00:07:13,400 --> 00:07:18,870
In a separate civil case, on 2 October
2013, a jury cleared the concert

110
00:07:18,910 --> 00:07:22,640
promoter AEG Live of negligence in
hiring Murray.

111
00:07:23,070 --> 00:07:27,210
So one man was convicted in the criminal
case, and the promoter was cleared in

112
00:07:27,250 --> 00:07:27,970
the civil one.

113
00:07:28,400 --> 00:07:34,440
On 28 October 2009, a film made from the
rehearsal footage opened in cinemas for

114
00:07:34,480 --> 00:07:35,600
a two week run.

115
00:07:36,030 --> 00:07:40,760
In March 2010, Sony signed a deal with
his estate, reported at two hundred and

116
00:07:40,800 --> 00:07:44,350
fifty million dollars, to keep
distributing his recordings.

117
00:07:44,770 --> 00:07:49,710
In 2015, Thriller became the first album
certified for thirty million shipments

118
00:07:49,750 --> 00:07:51,050
in the United States.

